  "description": "The partition function whose Mayer expansion has the corpus b3 as its third Ursell coefficient is the hard-core lattice gas on the nucleon sites with pair weight mu_e = tr(interface letter), grand-canonical over the sub-clusters of a fixed nucleus: Xi_S(z) = SUM_T z^T PROD_{e in T} mu_e, ln Xi_S = SUM_T z^T phi^T_T. The corpus cumulants are Boolean-lattice inversions of 1 - Z and equal -phi^T_n exactly while n <= 3 (no disconnected isolated-vertex-free graph below 4 vertices); at n = 4 they differ by the 3 perfect matchings. The Mayer coefficients of B = -alpha ln(Xi/Xi_free) are -phi^T_T at every order, so the corpus's negative b3 IS the classical sign; the 2026-08-30 'restore (-1)^(n-1)' prescription is the same expansion at negative activity and names no ensemble. Fixed-A (canonical) binding -alpha ln Z_S is exactly pairwise. No production letter has trace > 1, so no attractive Mayer channel is present (scope a).",
